.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/108459","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/108459","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/108459.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/108459.patch","merged_at":"2025-07-10T16:49:54Z"},"body":"Fixes #108435.\r\n\r\nUsing a const reference here seems reasonable at a glance, but there's actually a swap operation that can happen in the loop body that causes the partitioning to be incorrect. This doesn't seem to actually cause incorrectness in practice, because there's a final insertion sort pass, but it does degrade the sort's performance as a result.\r\n\r\nThis was originally not a const reference before #106661, so this isn't introducing anything new, just fixing it to match the old behavior.\r\n\r\nAs a bit more proof, here's a HotSpot flamegraph for 108435:\r\n![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/7519b60f-5648-4ad3-88ae-ed1f813e9381)\r\nThe large SortArray blocks are all in the `final_insertion_sort`, which ends up needing to sort the array itself.","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_